From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Settings' Files card without Google Drive, OneDrive
 and Microsoft 365

Cloud storage (patch 0050, nickel-cloud through rclone) takes their place
at the top of Settings > System preferences > Files: Google Drive's row
(DriveFS, which needs a Google account NickelOS doesn't sign in with) is
gone, and the OneDrive and Microsoft 365 rows are never shown. Their search
tags go too; "Cloud storage", "Google Drive", "OneDrive", "Dropbox" and
"Add cloud account" find the cloud storage accounts instead. The pages
themselves stay, reachable by their URLs only.

